{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22787 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "Khrinone C is implicated in the target engagement of the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a key enzyme in the sialylation pathway. This enzyme is also a target of two other compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate. These compounds are both known to interact with Replicase polyprotein 1ab, suggesting a potential role in the regulation of viral replication. The evidence indicates that Khrinone C may act through a shared pathway involving sialylation and metabolic intermediates, potentially influencing viral protein synthesis. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Khrinone C could modulate the replicase polyprotein 1ab, though the exact molecular mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
